{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1726","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Mainak and Interesting Sequence"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Mainak has two positive integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Mainak finds a sequence $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ of $$$n$$$ positive integers "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"interesting"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"for all"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers $$$i$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$), the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#XOR"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise XOR"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of all elements in $$$a$$$ which are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"strictly less"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" than $$$a_i$$$ is $$$0$$$. Formally if $$$p_i$$$ is the bitwise XOR of all elements in $$$a$$$ which are strictly less than $$$a_i$$$, then $$$a$$$ is an "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"interesting"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" sequence if $$$p_1 = p_2 = \\ldots = p_n = 0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, sequences $$$[1,3,2,3,1,2,3]$$$, $$$[4,4,4,4]$$$, $$$[25]$$$ are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"interesting"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", whereas $$$[1,2,3,4]$$$ ($$$p_2 = 1 \\ne 0$$$), $$$[4,1,1,2,4]$$$ ($$$p_1 = 1 \\oplus 1 \\oplus 2 = 2 \\ne 0$$$), $$$[29,30,30]$$$ ($$$p_2 = 29 \\ne 0$$$) aren't interesting."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Here $$$a \\oplus b$$$ denotes bitwise XOR of integers $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find any "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"interesting"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" sequence $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ (or report that there exists no such sequence) such that the sum of the elements in the sequence $$$a$$$ is equal to $$$m$$$, i.e. $$$a_1 + a_2 \\ldots + a_n = m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As a reminder, the bitwise XOR of an empty sequence is considered to be $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^5$$$) — the number of test cases. Description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line and the only line of each test case contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^5$$$, $$$1 \\le m \\le 10^9$$$) — the length of the sequence and the sum of the elements."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, if there exists some interesting sequence, output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" on the first line, otherwise output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"No"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". You may print each letter in any case (for example, \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will all be recognized as positive answer)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If the answer is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", output $$$n$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"positive integers"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$a_i \\ge 1$$$), forming an "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"interesting"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" sequence such that $$$a_1 + a_2 \\ldots + a_n = m$$$. If there are multiple solutions, output any."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n1 3\n6 12\n2 1\n3 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYes\n3\nYes\n1 3 2 2 3 1\nNo\nYes\n2 2 2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" In the first test case, $$$[3]$$$ is the only interesting sequence of length $$$1$$$ having sum $$$3$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" In the third test case, there is no sequence of length $$$2$$$ having sum of elements equal to $$$1$$$, so there is no such interesting sequence."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" In the fourth test case, $$$p_1 = p_2 = p_3 = 0$$$, because bitwise XOR of an empty sequence is $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1726B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1726/problem/B"}